							<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">100+ domestic landmarks (airports, data centres, landmarks)</td>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">International B2B export projects; references provided on inquiry</td>
						</tr>
					</tbody>
				</table>
			</div>

			<h2 id="quality-and-certifications" class="text-2xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-12 mb-4 tracking-tight scroll-mt-24">4. Quality Systems &amp; Certifications</h2>
			<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4"><strong>CA-FIRE</strong> holds an FM Approvals listing for its sprinkler heads (FM 2030) — the single most valuable credential in North American and FM-insured projects — together with CCCF (GB 5135), ISO 9001/14001/45001 and PICC product-liability insurance. UL certification for heads and alarm check valves is in progress, which is exactly the right disclosure for a buyer to note: as of this writing, their UL status is <em>pending</em>, not granted.</p>
			<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4"><strong>Wanlian Fluid</strong> operates under an ISO 9001 quality-management system across its own lines and qualified partner capacity, with 100% per-unit shell pressure and air-leakage testing and export documentation (certificates, inspection and pressure-test records) coordinated with shipment. We do not hold FM or UL listings, and we do not claim them — for models designed to UL/FM specification, per-model documentation is confirmed at quotation.</p>
			<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>Practical advice:</strong> certifications are per-product and per-destination. If your spec requires FM-listed sprinkler heads, that narrows you to listed manufacturers (CA-FIRE included); for every other line item, compare per-unit test records, standard-matched reports and third-party inspection options rather than brand names. Our <a href="/guides/how-to-verify-chinese-valve-supplier/" class="text-brand-blue font-semibold hover:underline">Chinese supplier verification guide</a> and <a href="/guides/detect-fake-valves-fire-equipment-counterfeits/" class="text-brand-blue font-semibold hover:underline">fake-certificate detection guide</a> cover the checks in detail.</p>

			<h2 id="where-each-wins" class="text-2xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-12 mb-4 tracking-tight scroll-mt-24">5. Where Each Manufacturer Wins</h2>
			<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4"><strong>CA-FIRE wins when:</strong> the specification-critical item is an FM-approved sprinkler head (NFPA 13 / FM Global projects in North America, and GCC projects following NFPA-based codes); the project is sprinkler-centric (heads + alarm/deluge valves from one source); or you value a disclosed 13+ year history with a large domestic landmark project portfolio as reference base.</p>
			<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4"><strong>Wanlian Fluid wins when:</strong> the project centers on fire water monitors (ZDMS auto-tracking is a core line, not an accessory); the scope is a complete fire kit — monitors, alarm valves, hydrants, <a href="/products/adjustable-pressure-reducing-valve-500x/" class="text-brand-blue font-semibold hover:underline">500X pressure reducing valves</a>, fire hose, nozzles and extinguisher boxes — under one PO; you need hydraulic control valves that CA-FIRE does not publish; you want IoT smart hydrants for municipal networks; or your distribution market speaks Spanish, Russian, French or Arabic and you want OEM brand assets in those languages.</p>
			<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>They coexist well:</strong> nothing stops a large international contractor from specifying FM-listed heads from CA-FIRE and the balance of the bill of materials from Wanlian. The two factories compete most directly on alarm check valves, hydrants and monitors — and least on sprinkler-head listings vs. hydraulic control and accessories, which are simply different halves of the fire-equipment market.</p>

			<h2 id="cost-and-lead-time" class="text-2xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-12 mb-4 tracking-tight scroll-mt-24">6. Cost, Pricing Model &amp; Lead Time</h2>
			<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">Both factories are quote-on-inquiry with no public price lists, so unit-price claims from either side should be verified per specification. CA-FIRE markets a 24-hour quote turnaround; Wanlian Fluid commits to 12-hour responses — both are fast enough for tender timelines.</p>
			<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">The structural cost difference is scope: FM-listed heads carry a listing premium that shows up in any sprinkler-centric BOM, while non-listed items (valves, hydrants, monitors, hose, cabinets) are priced in the same Quanzhou cluster where both factories source castings, coatings and test rigs. For a mixed kit, the decisive number is usually <em>total landed cost per PO</em> — item count, consolidation into one shipment, one customs entry and one quality audit — and that is where a full-range supplier like Wanlian tends to win on the non-head line items, even in projects where the heads themselves come from a listed maker.</p>

			<h2 id="which-should-you-choose" class="text-2xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-12 mb-4 tracking-tight scroll-mt-24">7. Which One Should You Choose?</h2>
			<div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-xl border border-gray-200 p-6 my-5">
				<p class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3">Choose <strong class="text-brand-blue">CA-FIRE</strong> when:</p>
				<ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed space-y-2">
					<li>Your project is governed by FM Global or NFPA 13 and requires FM-listed sprinkler heads (their FM 2030 listing is the differentiator).</li>
					<li>The scope is sprinkler-centric: heads + wet alarm check valves + deluge valves from a single source.</li>
					<li>You want a disclosed 13+ year track record with a large domestic landmark portfolio (airports, data centres) as reference base.</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
			<div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-xl border border-gray-200 p-6 my-5">
				<p class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3">Choose <strong class="text-brand-red">Wanlian Fluid</strong> when:</p>
				<ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed space-y-2">
					<li>Fire water monitors are the centerpiece — especially <a href="/products/auto-tracking-jet-suppression-cannon-zdms/" class="text-brand-blue font-semibold hover:underline">ZDMS auto-tracking cannons</a> for tank farms, depots and open areas.</li>
					<li>You want a complete fire kit under one PO: monitors, alarm valves, hydrants, hydraulic control valves, hose, nozzles and extinguisher cabinets, with OEM branding.</li>
					<li>You need hydraulic control valves (500X/100X/F745X) or IoT smart hydrants — lines CA-FIRE does not publish.</li>
					<li>You distribute in Spanish-, Russian-, French- or Arabic-speaking markets and want localized brand assets and a 5-language technical site.</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
			<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">The fastest way to decide: write down (1) whether FM-listed sprinkler heads appear in your specification, (2) whether "fire water cannon" or "hydraulic control valve" appears anywhere in the scope, and (3) which language your end buyers work in. Point (1) favors CA-FIRE; points (2) and (3) favor Wanlian Fluid. For a broader supplier evaluation framework, see our <a href="/guides/b2b-valve-sourcing-checklist/" class="text-brand-blue font-semibold hover:underline">B2B valve sourcing checklist</a>, and for the North American brand question, our <a href="/guides/wanlian-fluid-vs-american-avk/" class="text-brand-blue font-semibold hover:underline">Wanlian Fluid vs American AVK</a> comparison.</p>

			<!-- FAQ Section -->
			<h2 id="faq" class="text-2xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-12 mb-6 tracking-tight scroll-mt-24">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
			<div class="space-y-4">
				{faq.map(item => (
					<details class="group bg-gray-50 rounded-xl border border-gray-100 p-5 open:border-brand-red/30">
						<summary class="flex justify-between items-center font-bold text-gray-800 cursor-pointer list-none">
							<span>{item.question}</span>
							<span class="text-brand-blue text-xl transition-transform group-open:rotate-45">+</span>
						</summary>
						<p class="mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed text-sm">{item.answer}</p>
					</details>
				))}
			</div>

			<!-- Sources -->
			<h2 id="sources" class="text-2xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-12 mb-4 tracking-tight scroll-mt-24">Sources</h2>
			<ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed space-y-1.5">
				<li>CA-FIRE — About (founding, facility size, staff, revenue, certifications, reference projects): <a href="https://www.ca-fire.com/about-us/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-brand-blue font-semibold hover:underline">ca-fire.com</a></li>
